fsimg 0.1.0 (unreleased)

Resource contexts account for memory and owned descriptors, enforce session
quotas, and report cancellation and structured errors. Bounded positional I/O
supports regular files, callbacks, fixed sinks, and nested slices. Private
platform tests exercise confinement and no-replace regular-file publication.

Metadata streams, fixed-record arrays, and bitsets share a bounded page cache
and spill to private scratch files. Stable external sorting uses bounded merge
heaps and an on-disk run registry. Logical and sampled physical scratch use are
reported separately; session work quotas and cancellation cover metadata work.

Private writer collection supports descriptor-relative source-tree scanning,
zero and provider sources, strict Unicode codecs, and explicit timestamp and
metadata validity contracts. External catalog ordering assigns stable IDs and
parent links, validates sibling collisions, and retains paged result records.
Source reopening validates identity and mount boundaries; one writer-owned
current source is released on completion, failure, or destruction.

FAT12, FAT16, and FAT32 readers provide header information, depth-first
enumeration, current-file content and range reads, and complete structural
verification with optional payload read-through. Directory prepasses reject
long-name/short-alias ambiguity. Allocation chains, directory ownership, random
access indexes, and global allocation verification use bounded resources.
Names use pinned CP437 and Unicode simple-uppercase tables; timestamps retain
wall-clock semantics. Reader and writer capabilities are reported independently.
